  "semantics": [
    "Hello and StreamHello are explicit protocol-five records. Unknown profiles, fingerprints, kinds or protocols refuse; no downgrade or legacy transport fallback.",
    "Hello binds the host, transport, child, bundle/version, full managed manifest digest and fresh host-issued token to an admitted private Startup. StreamHello additionally binds the separately admitted call ID.",
    "Tokens are exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters. A host must issue a fresh cryptographically random 256-bit token for each child; shape admission cannot establish entropy, freshness or one-use ownership. Token equality uses the shared constant-time primitive.",
    "Record handles own immutable canonical bytes. Startup and handshake bytes contain credentials and belong only on protected IPC; errors and object representations must not echo input values.",
    "Pure record admission and binding do not install, execute, consume a nonce, authorize an invocation or establish the original caller. The host retains current trust, signed selection, channel lifecycle, call admission and replay/uncertainty duties.",
    "This profile selects only managed/2 protocol-six startup and never reinterprets an issued protocol-five handshake. Record parsing and matching never grant an inference call or processing-domain permission."
  ]
